      "id": 2,
      "claim": "Lower shear stress may fall below the critical shear stress (τ_c) required to keep sediment particles in motion.",
      "evidence": "Shields criterion: particles are entrained only if τ > τ_c; τ decreases with v.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "When τ < τ_c, particles are no longer suspended and settle out of the flow (deposition).",
      "evidence": "Hjulström curve shows that at low velocities the transport capacity drops and deposition occurs for all but the finest particles.",
      "weight": 0.30,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Therefore, deposition of material in the stream increases as stream velocity decreases.",
      "evidence": "More particles settle per unit time when the flow cannot keep them in motion.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [3]
    }
  ],
